WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:20.309
"Ahh!" Nathan yelled when the masked figure jumped in front of them.

2
00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:25.358
Henry gasped. Maggie and Cole jumped back.

3
00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:28.028
But they were startled for only a second.

4
00:00:28.029 --> 00:00:31.564
The figure was just a kid in a pirate mask.

5
00:00:31.565 --> 00:00:35.632
"Sorry I scared you," the kid said, pulling off his mask.

6
00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:40.285
William grinned. "This is Luke," he told Henry and the others.

7
00:00:40.286 --> 00:00:42.689
"He's a friend from my old school."

8
00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:47.472
"You must like pirates as much as Nathan does," Henry said.

9
00:00:47.473 --> 00:00:52.025
Luke nodded eagerly. "That's one reason I like coming here.

10
00:00:52.026 --> 00:00:55.194
I love exploring Pirate Beach!"

11
00:00:55.195 --> 00:01:00.407
"Pirate Beach?" Nathan echoed. "That's what this place is called?"

12
00:01:00.408 --> 00:01:05.142
Anna rolled her eyes. "It's named after some stupid legend."

13
00:01:05.143 --> 00:01:07.745
"The legend isn't stupid," Luke said.

14
00:01:07.746 --> 00:01:11.031
"Pirates used to land their ships here all the time.

15
00:01:11.032 --> 00:01:14.104
Some people think they hid their treasure on this beach."

16
00:01:14.105 --> 00:01:17.155
"Wow!" Nathan looked impressed.

17
00:01:17.156 --> 00:01:20.436
"That sounds like something from a pirate movie.

18
00:01:20.437 --> 00:01:24.252
In fact, I just heard about a new movie coming out soon.

19
00:01:24.253 --> 00:01:31.758
It's called Revenge of the Pirate's Ghost," he added. "I'm dying to see it!"

20
00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:33.956
"Me too," Luke said.

21
00:01:33.957 --> 00:01:38.309
Just then William's parents hurried out of the house.

22
00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:41.603
"Welcome!" William's mother said.

23
00:01:41.604 --> 00:01:46.420
"We have an exciting weekend planned for you," added William's father.

24
00:01:46.421 --> 00:01:49.972
"How would you like to search for pirate booty?"

25
00:01:49.973 --> 00:01:53.871
"Booty?" Maggie said. "What's that?"

26
00:01:53.872 --> 00:01:57.746
"Booty is what pirates call treasure," Luke explained.

27
00:01:57.747 --> 00:02:02.398
He turned to William's parents. "Is it real pirates' booty?"

28
00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:08.510
William's mother smiled. "Not exactly. We've created a treasure hunt for you."

29
00:02:08.511 --> 00:02:11.129
"What?" William blurted out.

30
00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:15.118
"Cool!" Nathan and Luke said at the same time.

31
00:02:15.119 --> 00:02:19.061
"That sounds perfect for Nathan and Luke," said Cole.

32
00:02:19.062 --> 00:02:21.904
"They're both obsessed with pirates!"

33
00:02:21.905 --> 00:02:26.648
"What's the treasure?" Maggie blurted out. "Is it gold?"

34
00:02:26.649 --> 00:02:32.636
William's mother smiled. "You'll have to wait to see what the treasure is," she said.

35
00:02:32.637 --> 00:02:36.374
"But here's how the hunt will work: we'll give you a clue.

36
00:02:36.375 --> 00:02:39.532
You'll follow it to find a hidden treasure chest.

37
00:02:39.533 --> 00:02:43.706
Some booty will be hidden inside, along with your next clue."

38
00:02:43.707 --> 00:02:48.790
"At the end of the treasure hunt, you'll find a big surprise!" her husband finished.

39
00:02:48.791 --> 00:02:53.473
"Awesome!" Luke pumped his fist. "Let's get started!"

40
00:02:53.474 --> 00:02:58.389
Everyone else looked excited too. Well, not everyone.

41
00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.430
Henry noticed that William didn't even seem to be paying attention.

42
00:03:02.431 --> 00:03:04.982
He was staring out at the ocean.

43
00:03:04.983 --> 00:03:07.550
"Come on, Henry." Cole poked him in the arm.

44
00:03:07.551 --> 00:03:15.370
"It's time to find some pirate booty!"

45
00:03:15.371 --> 00:03:21.546
After Henry and his friends dropped their luggage inside the house, William's father handed the clue to Anna.

46
00:03:21.547 --> 00:03:27.928
"Have fun, kids. We'll see you at lunchtime."

47
00:03:27.929 --> 00:03:33.502
Outside, Nathan took the clue from Anna. "Let me see that," he said.

48
00:03:33.503 --> 00:03:36.733
"Luke and I are the pirate experts around here.

49
00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:40.607
I bet we can figure out where the first treasure is!"

50
00:03:40.608 --> 00:03:43.818
"Right," Luke agreed. "I think we should—"

51
00:03:43.819 --> 00:03:48.465
"Don't hog the map," Maggie said, snatching the paper away from Nathan.

52
00:03:48.466 --> 00:03:52.468
"Besides, we don't need pirate experts to find treasure.

53
00:03:52.469 --> 00:03:55.879
We need The Lemonade Detectives!"

54
00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.020
"The what?" Anna sounded curious.

55
00:03:59.021 --> 00:04:02.755
Cole started to tell her and Luke about the detective agency.

56
00:04:02.756 --> 00:04:06.500
But Henry was watching Nathan, who was scowling at Maggie.

57
00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:11.102
"You're not the only ones who can figure out clues," Nathan complained.

58
00:04:11.103 --> 00:04:14.990
"And you shouldn't grab stuff out of other people's hands."

59
00:04:14.991 --> 00:04:24.091
"Sorry," Maggie mumbled. She continued studying the map.

60
00:04:24.092 --> 00:04:28.628
"Doesn't it look like the first chest is hidden near those big pointy rocks?"

61
00:04:28.629 --> 00:04:32.562
Henry looked at the map and then down at the beach where Maggie was pointing.

62
00:04:32.563 --> 00:04:39.811
"I think you're right! Let's go look."

63
00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:43.150
They all ran down the beach toward the pointy rock formation.

64
00:04:43.151 --> 00:04:47.479
When they got closer, they spotted a man wandering along in the surf.

65
00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.436
"Who's that?" Cole asked.

66
00:04:49.437 --> 00:04:55.797
As the man approached, they could see he had a bristly, reddish-brown beard and twinkling blue eyes.

67
00:04:55.798 --> 00:04:58.403
"I don't know," William said.

68
00:04:58.404 --> 00:05:02.319
"But he shouldn't be here—this is private property."

69
00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:06.503
The stranger had overheard William.

70
00:05:06.504 --> 00:05:09.843
"Private property, hmm?" he said with a chuckle.

71
00:05:09.844 --> 00:05:15.939
"It's a good thing my ancestor, Captain Roger Redbeard, isn't alive to hear you say that."

72
00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:23.323
"Captain Roger Redbeard?" Nathan echoed. "That sounds like a pirate's name."

73
00:05:23.324 --> 00:05:28.570
The man chuckled again. "That's because he was a pirate.

74
00:05:28.571 --> 00:05:31.651
He's the one Pirate Beach is named after."

75
00:05:31.652 --> 00:05:37.893
"Cool!" Luke exclaimed. "Does that mean you're the relative of a real pirate?"

76
00:05:37.894 --> 00:05:40.255
"That's right." The man nodded.

77
00:05:40.256 --> 00:05:44.036
"I'm even named after him. You can call me Roger."

78
00:05:44.037 --> 00:05:47.989
Henry noticed that Maggie wasn't paying attention to Roger.

79
00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.286
She'd hurried ahead of everyone.

80
00:05:50.287 --> 00:05:53.876
She looked at the map again and then back down at the sand.

81
00:05:53.877 --> 00:05:57.988
Then she dropped to her knees and started to dig with her hands.

82
00:05:57.989 --> 00:06:02.620
"I bet the treasure is right around here!"
